TypeScript Lesson 12: Optional Properties & readonly 🔐
Aaj hum seekhenge ki object ki property ko optional kaise banate hain aur kisi property ko change hone se kaise rokte hain.
1. Optional Property (?)
Maan lo ek user ke paas name aur email hai. Lekin har user ka email available hona zaroori nahi.
type User = {
    name: string;
    email?: string;
};

let user1: User = {
    name: "Rahul",
    email: "rahul@gmail.com"
};

let user2: User = {
    name: "Amit"
};

console.log(user1);
console.log(user2);


Dono objects valid hain!
Samjho:
- name: string — name dena zaroori hai.
- email?: string — email dena optional hai.
- ? ka matlab property ho bhi sakti hai aur nahi bhi.
Agar tum name hi nahi doge, to TypeScript error dega.
2. Optional Property ko safely use karna
Optional property ki value undefined ho sakti hai, isliye use karne se pehle check karna achha hai.
type User = {
    name: string;
    email?: string;
};

function showUser(user: User): void {
    console.log(user.name);

    if (user.email !== undefined) {
        console.log(user.email.toUpperCase());
    } else {
        console.log("Email not provided");
    }
}

showUser({ name: "Rahul" });
showUser({ name: "Priya", email: "priya@gmail.com" });


Output:
Rahul
Email not provided
Priya
PRIYA@GMAIL.COM


Yahan condition check karti hai ki email available hai ya nahi. Available hone par hi toUpperCase() call hota hai.
3. readonly kya hota hai?
Maan lo employee ki ID create hone ke baad change nahi honi chahiye.
type Employee = {
    readonly id: number;
    name: string;
};

let employee: Employee = {
    id: 101,
    name: "Rahul"
};

employee.name = "Amit"; // Valid

// employee.id = 102;   // TypeScript error


Kyun?
- name normal property hai, isliye change ho sakta hai.
- id ke aage readonly hai, isliye banne ke baad usko dobara assign nahi kar sakte.
Yaad rakho: readonly TypeScript ke type checking ke waqt protection deta hai; ye apne aap runtime par object ko immutable nahi banata.
4. Optional aur readonly ek saath
Dono features ek hi property par bhi use ho sakte hain.
type Product = {
    readonly productId: number;
    name: string;
    description?: string;
};

let product: Product = {
    productId: 1,
    name: "Laptop"
};

product.name = "Gaming Laptop"; // Valid

// product.productId = 2;       // Error
// description dena optional hai


Yahan productId change nahi kar sakte, lekin description dena zaroori nahi hai.

